  "_README": "Authored search keywords for stencils/v4/_index.json. `libraries` maps a library id (library[].id in a stencil file) to keywords given to every row of that library; `templates` maps a template id to keywords for that template's rows. A row's keywords are its library's followed by its template's, de-duplicated. `containers.libraries` and `containers.ids` mark rows `container: true` (shapes meant to hold other shapes; the MCP layout lint treats them as groups, never as obstacles). generate-stencil-index.js VALIDATES this file and FAILS naming the problem when its shape is wrong or when an id or a library it names is not in the catalogue, so a renamed stencil breaks the index build rather than silently losing its keywords. Keys starting with _ are ignored.",

